      "Bot: Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is a technique that enables large language models (LLMs) to retrieve and incorporate new information from external data sources. It works by first retrieving relevant documents or data in response to a user query, then using both the query and the retrieved information to generate a factually accurate, context-aware response. RAG enhances the accuracy and reliability of generative AI models by grounding responses in verified, external data, reducing the risk of hallucinations. It connects LLMs with enterprise data, improving the accuracy, context, and relevance of AI responses.\n"
